- 1 X thread\par
- 1 LinkedIn post\par
- 1 checklist asset\par
\par
---\par
\par
## 9) Risk, Legal, and Ethics Guardrails\par
\par
Before publishing an incident:\par
- Verify with at least two credible sources where possible.\par
- Redact private/sensitive data.\par
- Avoid naming individuals unless already public and necessary.\par
- Label speculation clearly.\par
- Include correction policy in profile/bio or pinned post.\par
\par
Use this disclaimer pattern:\par
- "This analysis is based on publicly available information as of [date]."\par
\par
---\par
\par
## 10) Templates You Can Reuse\par
\par
### A) Episode Script Template\par
- **Hook:** "This AI agent did X. Everyone blamed Y. The real problem was Z."\par
- **Context:** Who/what/when.\par
- **Failure chain:** Step-by-step.\par
- **Root cause:** Technical and process causes.\par
- **Prevention:** 3 controls (design, policy, monitoring).\par
- **Closing:** One-sentence operator takeaway.\par
\par
### B) X Thread Template\par
1. Hook + stakes\par
2. What happened\par
3. Why it mattered\par
4. Technical failure point\par
5. Process failure point\par
6. The fix that would've prevented this\par
7. Checklist\par
8. CTA question\par
\par
### C) LinkedIn Post Template\par
- Hook line\par
- Short incident summary\par
- Why systems failed (3 bullets)\par
- Prevention checklist (3 bullets)\par
- Ask for perspective from practitioners\par
\par
